    "result_text": "All 32 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nOn successful owner create, the endpoint now emits an audit line via the `AUDIT` logger carrying the owner id, customerCode and registrationDate.\n\n**New function** \u2014 `AuditOwnerCreated.java`:\n```java\nprivate static final Logger AUDIT = LoggerFactory.getLogger(\"AUDIT\");\n\npublic void service(@Val Owner owner) {\n    AUDIT.info(\"Owner created id={} customerCode={} registrationDate={}\",\n            owner.getId(), owner.getCustomerCode(), owner.getRegistrationDate());\n}\n```\nIt reads the persisted `Owner` via `@Val`, so it sees the generated id, the assigned customerCode and the resolved registrationDate.\n\n**Wiring** \u2014 `owners.POST.yml`: inserted an `audit` step between `save` and `respond`, under the same `govern: [ transaction ]` as the rest of the write pipeline, so it runs only after a successful insert (`save \u2192 audit \u2192 respond`).\n\nSince `registrationDate` is a `LocalDate` and `owner.getId()` is the persisted id, the emitted line (`INFO AUDIT - Owner created id=11 customerCode=TOW-SUR-0001 registrationDate=2026-08-17`) contains all three values in the same textual form the JSON response returns, satisfying the Cp21 assertion. Full suite: **32/32 green**.",
